<section id="install">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="section-tag">Before you download</span>
      <h2>A few useful things to know.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item"><h3>Will it work on my Mac?</h3><p>WhatBattery requires an Apple Silicon Mac running macOS 14 or later. Battery health and sleep features are for Mac laptops; available readings vary by device. <a href="/docs/install/">Read the installation guide.</a></p></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><h3>Are overnight drain insights included for free?</h3><p>The Sleep tab is part of Pro. The free app includes Mac battery health, live battery power and supported accessory levels, so you can start there before choosing an upgrade.</p></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><h3>Does it change how my Mac charges?</h3><p>No. WhatBattery reads and explains the available information. It doesn’t enforce a charging limit or change your Mac’s charging settings.</p></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><h3>Does my battery history leave my Mac?</h3><p>History is stored locally. Optional wear comparison is off by default, and reports are saved where you choose. Licence activation and update checks use online services. <a href="/privacy/">Read the privacy details.</a></p></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><h3>How do I install it?</h3><p>Download the ZIP, drag WhatBattery into Applications and open it. The app is signed and notarised by Apple. <a href="/docs/install/">See the full guide and Homebrew option.</a></p></div>
